---
import Head from '../../layouts/Head.astro';
import SvgDefs from '../../components/SvgDefs.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import '../../styles/landing.css';
import '../../styles/backdrop.css';

const title = 'Demo — the same question, twice | coldstart';
const description =
  "Two real sessions against coldstart's own codebase. The first has no note yet and looks things up. The second is handed the answer before it starts. Fully rendered, nothing animated.";
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <Head
    title={title}
    description={description}
    keywords="coldstart demo, coldstart find, coldstart gs, notebook recall, codebase memory demo, AI coding agent navigation"
    canonicalPath="/demo/"
    ogType="website"
    ogTitle="Demo — the same question, twice"
    ogDescription="The first session looks it up. The second already knows. One real repo, real command output, nothing animated."
    themeColor="#070a11"
  />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;1,6..72,400;1,6..72,500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
</head>
<body>
<SvgDefs />
<Nav variant="demo" />

<header class="hero demo-hero">
  <div class="wrap hero-in">
    <div class="kicker">Demo — captured from this repo</div>
    <h1 class="title">The first time it looks things up.<br>The second time it already knows.</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">The same question, asked in two different sessions against coldstart's own codebase. Every command and every line of output below is real and unedited. Nothing here animates — it is all on the page already.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ============================ COLD ============================ -->
<section class="dsec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="dhead">
      <div class="eyebrow">Session one · nothing written down yet</div>
      <h2>No note exists. So it goes and looks.</h2>
      <p class="lead">The recall hook searches the notebook first and finds nothing, so the agent falls through to the index: one <code>find</code> to locate the file, one <code>gs</code> to see who uses it, then it answers.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cc">
      <div class="cc-bar"><span class="cc-file">coldstart-mcp</span><span class="cc-badge">Claude Code</span></div>
      <div class="cc-body">

        <div class="turn">
          <div class="g">IN</div>
          <div class="c"><div class="chip">why does <code>gs</code> show files edited together — is that from the import graph?</div></div>
        </div>

        <p class="cap">The notebook is searched before anything else. Nothing matches, so nothing is injected.</p>

        <div class="turn">
          <div class="g"></div>
          <div class="c"><div class="prose think">Nothing in the notebook covers this. I'll find where the co-change data is produced.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="turn">
          <div class="g">OUT</div>
          <div class="c">
            <div class="tool">
              <div class="th"><span class="dot ok"></span><b>Bash</b> <span class="arg">coldstart find edited together cochange sidecar</span></div>
              <div class="ob"><div>find: edited together cochange sidecar  (4 terms, 69 candidate files)</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>▸ hooks/cochange-nudge.mjs   [4/4]</div><div>   Role:  defines `edited`, `cochange`</div><div>   Wired: used by `cochange-nudge.test.ts` · near `cochange.ts`</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>▸ tests/cochange-nudge.test.ts   [3/4]</div><div>   Role:  defines `sidecar`; named for `cochange`</div><div>   Wired: uses `cochange-nudge.mjs`, `cochange.ts`</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>▸ src/indexer/cochange.ts   [3/4]</div><div>   Role:  named for `cochange`; defines `sidecar`</div><div class="el">… +38 lines</div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="cap">One command, no model call. The third hit is the source file — <code>gs</code> next, to see what actually feeds it.</p>

        <div class="turn">
          <div class="g">OUT</div>
          <div class="c">
            <div class="tool">
              <div class="th"><span class="dot ok"></span><b>Bash</b> <span class="arg">coldstart gs src/indexer/cochange.ts</span></div>
              <div class="ob"><div>src/indexer/cochange.ts (275 lines, importedBy: 8)</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Symbols:</div><div>constant CO_CHANGE_WINDOW [L38]</div><div>constant CO_CHANGE_MIN_SUPPORT [L46]</div><div>function parseCommits [L77-98]</div><div>function canonicalizeRenames [L114-129]</div><div>function deriveCoChange [L139-210]  ← src/index-manager.ts:233</div><div>function coChangePartnersFor [L257-274]  ← src/server/tools.ts:388</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Imports:</div><div>src/cache/disk-cache.ts</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Importers (8):</div><div>  Source (5):</div><div>    src/graph/dump.ts</div><div>    src/index-manager.ts</div><div>    src/server/tools.ts</div><div class="el">… +14 lines</div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="turn">
          <div class="g"></div>
          <div class="c"><div class="prose">No. It comes from git history, not the graph.<br><br><code>parseCommits</code> reads <code>git log --name-status -M</code> and <code>deriveCoChange</code> counts how often two files change in the same commit — a 12,000-commit window, minimum support 2. It never touches <code>Imports</code> or the call edges. <code>coChangePartnersFor</code> is what <code>src/server/tools.ts:388</code> calls to render the section.<br><br>So it is a habit, not a dependency. There is no edge to go looking for.</div></div>
        </div>

        <p class="cap">Two commands and an answer. What made it expensive was not knowing where to start.</p>

        <div class="turn">
          <div class="g"></div>
          <div class="c"><div class="hook"><span class="hl">Stop hook</span> the agent writes down what it just worked out — file, symbols, and the reason, checked against a content hash so it expires when the code moves.</div></div>
        </div>

      </div>
      <div class="cc-in"><span>Reply to Claude…</span><span class="send">↑</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================ WARM ============================ -->
<section class="dsec warm">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="dhead">
      <div class="eyebrow">Session two · days later, fresh context</div>
      <h2>Same question. The answer arrives before it starts.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Different session, no memory of the first. The recall hook matches the note this time and hands it over with the prompt, so there is nothing left to look up.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cc">
      <div class="cc-bar"><span class="cc-file">coldstart-mcp</span><span class="cc-badge">Claude Code</span></div>
      <div class="cc-body">

        <div class="turn">
          <div class="g">IN</div>
          <div class="c"><div class="chip">is the "edited together" list in <code>gs</code> a dependency edge?</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="turn">
          <div class="g"></div>
          <div class="c">
            <div class="note">
              <div class="nh"><span class="nlbl">From the notebook</span><span class="fresh">fresh</span></div>
              <div class="nt">Co-change is git history, not the import graph</div>
              <div class="nb2">Pairs come from <code>git log --name-status -M</code> counted over a 12k-commit window in <code>deriveCoChange</code>, min support 2. Renames are carried forward over the whole window, because <code>-M</code> only labels the rename commit. It is a habit, NOT a dependency edge — there is no import or call relation behind it.</div>
              <div class="na">src/indexer/cochange.ts · deriveCoChange, coChangePartnersFor</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="cap">Verified against the file's content hash. <code>fresh</code> means <code>cochange.ts</code> has not changed a byte since this was written, so it can be trusted without re-reading.</p>

        <div class="turn">
          <div class="g"></div>
          <div class="c"><div class="prose">No — it is a habit, not a dependency.<br><br>The pairs are counted from git history in <code>deriveCoChange</code>, over a 12,000-commit window with a minimum support of 2. Nothing in it consults the import graph or the call edges, so a file listed there may have no code relation to the one you asked about at all. It is answering "what do people usually change alongside this", which is often the test in another language or the doc that has to stay in sync.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="turn">
          <div class="g"></div>
          <div class="c"><div class="tally"><b>Zero tool calls.</b> No <code>find</code>, no <code>gs</code>, no reads. The second session did not pay for the first session's search.</div></div>
        </div>

      </div>
      <div class="cc-in"><span>Reply to Claude…</span><span class="send">↑</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="dclose">
      <p class="big">The notebook is the difference between the two panels.</p>
      <p class="sm">Both sessions had the index. Only the second had the note — and it is the note that removed the work.</p>
      <div class="cta"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/">Read the docs →</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/docs/notebook/">How the notebook works</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<Footer />
</body>
</html>

<style is:global>
/* ---------- demo page shell ---------- */
.demo-hero{padding:44px 0 8px;}
.demo-hero .title{font-size:clamp(30px,4.6vw,48px);}
.dsec{padding:72px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);}
.dsec.warm{border-top-color:var(--line-warm);}
.dhead{max-width:640px;margin:0 auto 44px;text-align:center;}
.dhead h2{margin-top:14px;}
.dhead .lead{margin-top:16px;max-width:500px;margin-inline:auto;}

/* ---------- the Claude Code panel — a replica, on its own neutral ground ---------- */
.cc{max-width:880px;margin:0 auto;background:#1f1f1f;border:1px solid #2f2f2f;border-radius:10px;
  overflow:hidden;text-align:left;box-shadow:0 24px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.42);}
.cc-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;
  padding:11px 16px;background:#252525;border-bottom:1px solid #333;}
.cc-file{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:#8a8a8a;}
.cc-badge{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:#8a8a8a;border:1px solid #3a3a3a;border-radius:4px;padding:3px 7px;}
.cc-body{padding:22px 20px 8px;}

.turn{display:grid;grid-template-columns:34px 1fr;gap:14px;align-items:start;margin-bottom:18px;}
.turn > .g{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#6e6e6e;
  text-align:right;padding-top:9px;}
.turn > .c{min-width:0;}

.chip{background:#2e2e2e;border-radius:6px;padding:10px 14px;color:#f2f2f2;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.55;}
.prose{color:#e3e3e3;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.65;padding:2px 2px;}
.prose.think{color:#9a9a9a;font-style:italic;}
.cc code{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12.5px;color:#d9a05b;
  background:rgba(255,255,255,.06);border-radius:4px;padding:1px 5px;}

.tool{border:1px solid #383838;border-radius:6px;background:#1a1a1a;overflow:hidden;}
.th{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:9px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid #2c2c2c;
  font-size:13px;color:#f2f2f2;flex-wrap:wrap;}
.th b{font-weight:600;}
.th .arg{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:#8a8a8a;}
.dot{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;flex:none;background:#6b6b6b;}
.dot.ok{background:#7ec89a;}
.ob{padding:11px 12px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;color:#cfcfcf;
  overflow-x:auto;}
.ob > div{white-space:pre;}
.ob .el{color:#6e6e6e;}

/* the note, as the recall hook hands it over */
.note{border:1px solid rgba(239,148,72,.34);border-radius:6px;background:rgba(239,148,72,.05);padding:14px 15px;}
.nh{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:9px;}
.nlbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#d9a05b;}
.fresh{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#7ec89a;
  border:1px solid rgba(126,200,154,.4);border-radius:4px;padding:2px 6px;}
.nt{font-family:var(--display);font-size:17px;color:#f2f2f2;margin-bottom:8px;}
.nb2{font-size:13px;line-height:1.62;color:#cfcfcf;}
.na{margin-top:10px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:#8a8a8a;}

.hook{border-left:2px solid #7ec89a;padding:4px 0 4px 12px;font-size:12.5px;color:#9a9a9a;line-height:1.6;}
.hook .hl{color:#7ec89a;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.06em;
  text-transform:uppercase;margin-right:8px;}
.tally{border:1px dashed #3a3a3a;border-radius:6px;padding:11px 13px;font-size:13px;color:#cfcfcf;line-height:1.6;}
.tally b{color:#f2f2f2;font-weight:600;}

.cc-in{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;margin:6px 16px 16px;
  background:#242424;border:1px solid rgba(239,148,72,.45);border-radius:8px;padding:11px 13px;
  font-size:13px;color:#6e6e6e;}
.cc-in .send{width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:5px;background:#a8604a;color:#fff;
  display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:12px;}

/* captions sit outside the replica so the panel carries no marketing copy */
.cap{max-width:600px;margin:-4px auto 20px;padding:0 4px;text-align:center;
  font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--faint);}
.cap code{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ember);background:none;padding:0;}

.dclose{max-width:600px;margin:56px auto 0;text-align:center;}
.dclose .big{font-family:var(--display);font-size:clamp(20px,2.6vw,26px);color:var(--text);line-height:1.35;}
.dclose .sm{margin-top:12px;font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;}
.dclose .cta{margin-top:28px;justify-content:center;}

@media(max-width:720px){
  .cc-body{padding:18px 12px 6px;}
  .turn{grid-template-columns:22px 1fr;gap:9px;}
  .turn > .g{font-size:9px;}
  .ob{font-size:11px;}
}
</style>
